# Each line makes a figure of its own: `Chart.line` calls `plt.subplots()` itself, whatever the chart holds, so two
# lines meant for one chart are two figures. In a notebook each is on the screen, named by the call that made it, since
# nothing beyond the call holds it; elsewhere both rest in pyplot's figure. `fig` is dropped; `ax` is drawn on by the
# body itself (`ax.plot(..)`), and the chart is only read (`self.title`), so the chart the route returns is the one it
# built.

route notebooks.compare
step compare/compare
step compare/compare/Chart()
step compare/compare/Chart.line
step compare/compare/Chart.line/subplots                                                            # `fig, ax = plt.subplots()`
step compare/compare/Chart.line#2
step compare/compare/Chart.line#2/subplots

line entry > compare call
line compare/compare/Chart() > Chart·chart@compare/compare/Chart() value
line Chart·chart@compare/compare/Chart() > compare/compare/Chart.line value                         # `self.title`
line compare/compare/Chart.line/subplots > _·fig@compare/compare/Chart.line/subplots value
line compare/compare/Chart.line/subplots > _·ax@compare/compare/Chart.line/subplots value
line _·ax@compare/compare/Chart.line/subplots > compare/compare/Chart.line value          # `ax.plot(..)`
line compare/compare/Chart.line > Figure 1 · Chart.line own
line Chart·chart@compare/compare/Chart() > compare/compare/Chart.line#2 value
line compare/compare/Chart.line#2/subplots > _·fig@compare/compare/Chart.line#2/subplots value
line compare/compare/Chart.line#2/subplots > _·ax@compare/compare/Chart.line#2/subplots value
line _·ax@compare/compare/Chart.line#2/subplots > compare/compare/Chart.line#2 value
line compare/compare/Chart.line#2 > Figure 2 · Chart.line own                                       # a second figure
line Chart·chart@compare/compare/Chart() > compare/compare value                         # `return chart`
line compare/compare > Chart·chart@compare/compare value

home Chart·chart@compare/compare/Chart() compare/compare
home _·fig@compare/compare/Chart.line/subplots compare/compare/Chart.line
home _·ax@compare/compare/Chart.line/subplots compare/compare/Chart.line
home _·fig@compare/compare/Chart.line#2/subplots compare/compare/Chart.line#2
home _·ax@compare/compare/Chart.line#2/subplots compare/compare/Chart.line#2
home Chart·chart@compare/compare compare

side entry left
side Figure 1 · Chart.line right
side Figure 2 · Chart.line right

route charts.chart.compare
step compare/Chart()
step compare/Chart.line
step compare/Chart.line/subplots
step compare/Chart.line#2
step compare/Chart.line#2/subplots

line entry > compare call
line compare/Chart() > Chart·chart@compare/Chart() value
line Chart·chart@compare/Chart() > compare/Chart.line value
line compare/Chart.line/subplots > _·fig@compare/Chart.line/subplots value
line compare/Chart.line/subplots > _·ax@compare/Chart.line/subplots value
line _·ax@compare/Chart.line/subplots > compare/Chart.line value
line compare/Chart.line > Figure own
line Chart·chart@compare/Chart() > compare/Chart.line#2 value
line compare/Chart.line#2/subplots > _·fig@compare/Chart.line#2/subplots value
line compare/Chart.line#2/subplots > _·ax@compare/Chart.line#2/subplots value
line _·ax@compare/Chart.line#2/subplots > compare/Chart.line#2 value
line compare/Chart.line#2 > Figure own
line Chart·chart@compare/Chart() > compare value
line compare > Chart@compare value

home Chart·chart@compare/Chart() compare
home _·fig@compare/Chart.line/subplots compare/Chart.line
home _·ax@compare/Chart.line/subplots compare/Chart.line
home _·fig@compare/Chart.line#2/subplots compare/Chart.line#2
home _·ax@compare/Chart.line#2/subplots compare/Chart.line#2
home Chart@compare compare

side entry left
side Figure right
